   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Topological Majorana VAE Demo\n",
    "\n",
    "This English-language notebook demonstrates a compact, reproducible research workflow inspired by the original **Topological-Majorana-VAE** concept.\n",
    "\n",
    "It includes:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. A reliable `initial_quantum_state` initialization\n",
    "2. Hilbert-space normalization and Hermiticity checks\n",
    "3. Majorana-inspired operators and a toy Hamiltonian\n",
    "4. A Variational Autoencoder (VAE) latent-space example\n",
    "5. Latent-space clustering and reconstruction inspection\n",
    "6. Relativistic and thermal decoherence as a conceptual toy model\n",
    "7. Classical tabular Q-learning for state-conditioning actions\n",
    "8. A full visualization dashboard\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Scientific scope:** Matrix functions, state normalization, density matrices, Pauli operators, Lorentz factors, and VAE/Q-learning algorithms are standard mathematical or computational tools. The combined Majorana/deep-space decoherence score and irrational perturbation rules used here are illustrative models, not validated predictions for physical hardware.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Environment setup\n",
    "\n",
    "The main demo uses NumPy, SciPy, scikit-learn, Matplotlib, and Seaborn. The VAE section uses PyTorch. If PyTorch is unavailable, install it in the notebook environment and restart the kernel.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Uncomment if PyTorch is not installed in your notebook environment:\n",
    "# %pip install torch\n",
    "\n",
    "import math\n",
    "import random\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "from dataclasses import dataclass\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import scipy.linalg as la\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    import torch\n",
    "    import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "    from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, TensorDataset\n",
    "    TORCH_AVAILABLE = True\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    TORCH_AVAILABLE = False\n",
    "\n",
    "SEED = 42\n",
    "np.random.seed(SEED)\n",
    "random.seed(SEED)\n",
    "if TORCH_AVAILABLE:\n",
    "    torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n",
    "print(\"PyTorch available:\", TORCH_AVAILABLE)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Constants and initial-state creation\n",
    "\n",
    "Creating the state through a function removes the notebook-order dependency that caused:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "NameError: name 'initial_quantum_state' is not defined\n",
    "```\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "C = 299_792_458.0\n",
    "H_BAR = 1.054_571_817e-34\n",
    "K_B = 1.380_649e-23\n",
    "ALPHA = 1 / 137.035999\n",
    "T_ZERO = 2.725\n",
    "PI = np.pi\n",
    "PHI = (1 + np.sqrt(5)) / 2\n",
    "E = np.e\n",
    "SQRT2 = np.sqrt(2)\n",
    "GAMMA = 0.5772156649\n",
    "\n",
    "class HilbertSpaceCorrection:\n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def normalize_hilbert(psi, eps=1e-12):\n",
    "        psi = np.asarray(psi, dtype=np.complex128)\n",
    "        norm = np.linalg.norm(psi.ravel())\n",
    "        if norm < eps:\n",
    "            raise ValueError(\"Cannot normalize a zero state.\")\n",
    "        return psi / norm\n",
    "\n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def enforce_hermiticity(matrix):\n",
    "        matrix = np.asarray(matrix, dtype=np.complex128)\n",
    "        if matrix.ndim != 2 or matrix.shape[0] != matrix.shape[1]:\n",
    "            raise ValueError(\"Hermiticity requires a square matrix.\")\n",
    "        return 0.5 * (matrix + matrix.conj().T)\n",
    "\n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def state_validity_check(psi, atol=1e-8):\n",
    "        psi = np.asarray(psi)\n",
    "        norm = float(np.linalg.norm(psi.ravel()))\n",
    "        hermitian = None\n",
    "        if psi.ndim == 2 and psi.shape[0] == psi.shape[1]:\n",
    "            hermitian = bool(np.allclose(psi, psi.conj().T, atol=atol))\n",
    "        return {\"valid_norm\": bool(np.isclose(norm, 1.0, atol=atol)),\n",
    "                \"norm\": norm, \"hermitian\": hermitian,\n",
    "                \"finite\": bool(np.isfinite(psi).all())}\n",
    "\n",
    "def create_initial_quantum_state(dimension=4, seed=SEED, hermitian=False):\n",
    "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n",
    "    state = (rng.normal(0.5, 0.2, (dimension, dimension))\n",
    "             + 1j * rng.normal(0.1, 0.1, (dimension, dimension)))\n",
    "    if hermitian:\n",
    "        state = HilbertSpaceCorrection.enforce_hermiticity(state)\n",
    "    return HilbertSpaceCorrection.normalize_hilbert(state)\n",
    "\n",
    "initial_quantum_state = create_initial_quantum_state()\n",
    "initial_validation = HilbertSpaceCorrection.state_validity_check(initial_quantum_state)\n",
    "prob_density_array = np.abs(initial_quantum_state) ** 2\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Shape:\", initial_quantum_state.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Validation:\", initial_validation)\n",
    "print(\"Probability sum:\", prob_density_array.sum())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Majorana-inspired operators\n",
    "\n",
    "For `n` fermionic sites, this implementation creates `2n` Hermitian operators through a Jordan-Wigner construction. They satisfy the Majorana anticommutation relation numerically.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class MajoranaQuantumState:\n",
    "    X = np.array([[0, 1], [1, 0]], dtype=np.complex128)\n",
    "    Y = np.array([[0, -1j], [1j, 0]], dtype=np.complex128)\n",
    "    Z = np.array([[1, 0], [0, -1]], dtype=np.complex128)\n",
    "    I = np.eye(2, dtype=np.complex128)\n",
    "\n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def _kron_all(items):\n",
    "        result = np.array([[1]], dtype=np.complex128)\n",
    "        for item in items:\n",
    "            result = np.kron(result, item)\n",
    "        return result\n",
    "\n",
    "    @classmethod\n",
    "    def majorana_operators(cls, n_sites=2):\n",
    "        operators = []\n",
    "        for site in range(n_sites):\n",
    "            prefix = [cls.Z] * site\n",
    "            suffix = [cls.I] * (n_sites - site - 1)\n",
    "            operators.append(cls._kron_all(prefix + [cls.X] + suffix))\n",
    "            operators.append(cls._kron_all(prefix + [cls.Y] + suffix))\n",
    "        return operators\n",
    "\n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def majorana_hamiltonian(gamma_ops, coupling=0.1):\n",
    "        H = np.zeros_like(gamma_ops[0])\n",
    "        for i in range(len(gamma_ops) - 1):\n",
    "            H += 1j * coupling * gamma_ops[i] @ gamma_ops[i + 1]\n",
    "        return HilbertSpaceCorrection.enforce_hermiticity(H)\n",
    "\n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def superposition(gamma_ops, coefficients):\n",
    "        state = sum(c * op[:, 0] for c, op in zip(coefficients, gamma_ops))\n",
    "        return HilbertSpaceCorrection.normalize_hilbert(state)\n",
    "\n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def pure_state_entropy(state):\n",
    "        state = HilbertSpaceCorrection.normalize_hilbert(state).ravel()\n",
    "        rho = np.outer(state, state.conj())\n",
    "        eigvals = np.linalg.eigvalsh(rho)\n",
    "        eigvals = eigvals[eigvals > 1e-12]\n",
    "        return float(-np.sum(eigvals * np.log2(eigvals)))\n",
    "\n",
    "gamma_ops = MajoranaQuantumState.majorana_operators(n_sites=2)\n",
    "majorana_hamiltonian = MajoranaQuantumState.majorana_hamiltonian(gamma_ops)\n",
    "majorana_state = MajoranaQuantumState.superposition(\n",
    "    gamma_ops, [0.5 + 0.1j, 0.3j, 0.2 - 0.1j, 0.4 + 0.2j]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "anticommutator_error = 0.0\n",
    "identity = np.eye(gamma_ops[0].shape[0])\n",
    "for i, gi in enumerate(gamma_ops):\n",
    "    for j, gj in enumerate(gamma_ops):\n",
    "        target = 2 * identity if i == j else np.zeros_like(identity)\n",
    "        anticommutator_error = max(\n",
    "            anticommutator_error,\n",
    "            np.linalg.norm(gi @ gj + gj @ gi - target)\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Operators:\", len(gamma_ops))\n",
    "print(\"Hamiltonian Hermitian:\", np.allclose(majorana_hamiltonian, majorana_hamiltonian.conj().T))\n",
    "print(\"Maximum anticommutator error:\", anticommutator_error)\n",
    "print(\"Pure-state entropy:\", MajoranaQuantumState.pure_state_entropy(majorana_state))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Synthetic topological-array dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "The following dataset is synthetic. Each sample is an `8 \u00d7 8` matrix generated from one of six wave/topology-inspired templates with noise. The labels are used only to color the final plots, not to train the VAE.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def generate_topological_dataset(samples=1200, size=8, clusters=6, seed=SEED):\n",
    "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n",
    "    x = np.linspace(-1, 1, size)\n",
    "    Xg, Yg = np.meshgrid(x, x)\n",
    "    data, labels = [], []\n",
    "\n",
    "    for i in range(samples):\n",
    "        label = i % clusters\n",
    "        phase = rng.uniform(0, 2 * np.pi)\n",
    "        freq = 1 + label * 0.35\n",
    "        if label == 0:\n",
    "            base = np.sin(freq * np.pi * Xg + phase)\n",
    "        elif label == 1:\n",
    "            base = np.cos(freq * np.pi * Yg + phase)\n",
    "        elif label == 2:\n",
    "            base = np.sin(np.pi * freq * (Xg + Yg) + phase)\n",
    "        elif label == 3:\n",
    "            radius = np.sqrt(Xg**2 + Yg**2)\n",
    "            base = np.cos(freq * 2 * np.pi * radius + phase)\n",
    "        elif label == 4:\n",
    "            base = np.tanh(3 * Xg * Yg) + 0.3 * np.sin(freq * np.pi * Xg)\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            angle = np.arctan2(Yg, Xg)\n",
    "            radius = np.sqrt(Xg**2 + Yg**2)\n",
    "            base = np.sin(3 * angle + freq * np.pi * radius + phase)\n",
    "        noisy = base + rng.normal(0, 0.12, base.shape)\n",
    "        noisy = (noisy - noisy.min()) / (noisy.max() - noisy.min() + 1e-12)\n",
    "        data.append(noisy)\n",
    "        labels.append(label)\n",
    "    return np.asarray(data, dtype=np.float32), np.asarray(labels)\n",
    "\n",
    "matrix_data, topology_labels = generate_topological_dataset()\n",
    "flat_data = matrix_data.reshape(len(matrix_data), -1)\n",
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    flat_data, topology_labels, test_size=0.2, random_state=SEED, stratify=topology_labels\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"Dataset:\", matrix_data.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Train/Test:\", X_train.shape, X_test.shape)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Variational Autoencoder\n",
    "\n",
    "The VAE learns a two-dimensional probabilistic latent representation. The loss combines reconstruction error with Kullback-Leibler regularization.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if TORCH_AVAILABLE:\n",
    "    class VAE(nn.Module):\n",
    "        def __init__(self, input_dim=64, hidden_dim=32, latent_dim=2):\n",
    "            super().__init__()\n",
    "            self.encoder = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(input_dim, hidden_dim), nn.ReLU())\n",
    "            self.mu = nn.Linear(hidden_dim, latent_dim)\n",
    "            self.logvar = nn.Linear(hidden_dim, latent_dim)\n",
    "            self.decoder = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "                nn.Linear(latent_dim, hidden_dim), nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "                nn.Linear(hidden_dim, input_dim), nn.Sigmoid()\n",
    "            )\n",
    "\n",
    "        def encode(self, x):\n",
    "            h = self.encoder(x)\n",
    "            return self.mu(h), self.logvar(h)\n",
    "\n",
    "        @staticmethod\n",
    "        def reparameterize(mu, logvar):\n",
    "            std = torch.exp(0.5 * logvar)\n",
    "            return mu + torch.randn_like(std) * std\n",
    "\n",
    "        def forward(self, x):\n",
    "            mu, logvar = self.encode(x)\n",
    "            z = self.reparameterize(mu, logvar)\n",
    "            return self.decoder(z), mu, logvar\n",
    "\n",
    "    def vae_loss(reconstruction, x, mu, logvar, beta=0.01):\n",
    "        reconstruction_loss = nn.functional.mse_loss(reconstruction, x, reduction=\"sum\")\n",
    "        kl = -0.5 * torch.sum(1 + logvar - mu.pow(2) - logvar.exp())\n",
    "        return reconstruction_loss + beta * kl, reconstruction_loss, kl\n",
    "\n",
    "    device = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n",
    "    vae = VAE().to(device)\n",
    "    optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(vae.parameters(), lr=1e-3)\n",
    "    train_loader = DataLoader(\n",
    "        TensorDataset(torch.tensor(X_train, dtype=torch.float32)),\n",
    "        batch_size=64, shuffle=True\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    history = {\"loss\": [], \"reconstruction\": [], \"kl\": []}\n",
    "    epochs = 40\n",
    "    for epoch in range(epochs):\n",
    "        totals = np.zeros(3)\n",
    "        vae.train()\n",
    "        for (batch,) in train_loader:\n",
    "            batch = batch.to(device)\n",
    "            optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
    "            reconstruction, mu, logvar = vae(batch)\n",
    "            loss, rec, kl = vae_loss(reconstruction, batch, mu, logvar)\n",
    "            loss.backward()\n",
    "            optimizer.step()\n",
    "            totals += [loss.item(), rec.item(), kl.item()]\n",
    "        history[\"loss\"].append(totals[0] / len(X_train))\n",
    "        history[\"reconstruction\"].append(totals[1] / len(X_train))\n",
    "        history[\"kl\"].append(totals[2] / len(X_train))\n",
    "\n",
    "    vae.eval()\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        test_tensor = torch.tensor(X_test, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n",
    "        test_reconstruction, test_mu, test_logvar = vae(test_tensor)\n",
    "        latent_points = test_mu.cpu().numpy()\n",
    "        reconstructed_test = test_reconstruction.cpu().numpy()\n",
    "\n",
    "    kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=6, random_state=SEED, n_init=20)\n",
    "    latent_clusters = kmeans.fit_predict(latent_points)\n",
    "    latent_silhouette = silhouette_score(latent_points, latent_clusters)\n",
    "    test_mse = float(np.mean((reconstructed_test - X_test) ** 2))\n",
    "    print(f\"Device: {device}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Test reconstruction MSE: {test_mse:.6f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Latent K-means silhouette: {latent_silhouette:.4f}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    history = {\"loss\": [], \"reconstruction\": [], \"kl\": []}\n",
    "    pca = PCA(n_components=2, random_state=SEED)\n",
    "    latent_points = pca.fit_transform(X_test)\n",
    "    reconstructed_test = pca.inverse_transform(latent_points)\n",
    "    kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=6, random_state=SEED, n_init=20)\n",
    "    latent_clusters = kmeans.fit_predict(latent_points)\n",
    "    latent_silhouette = silhouette_score(latent_points, latent_clusters)\n",
    "    test_mse = float(np.mean((reconstructed_test - X_test) ** 2))\n",
    "    warnings.warn(\"PyTorch not found. PCA fallback used so the visualization remains runnable.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Relativistic decoherence toy model\n",
    "\n",
    "This section combines a Lorentz factor with an illustrative thermal suppression rule. It is useful for software experimentation, but it is not a calibrated model of a physical Majorana device.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class RelativisticDecoherence:\n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def lorentz_factor(velocity):\n",
    "        if abs(velocity) >= C:\n",
    "            raise ValueError(\"Velocity magnitude must be below the speed of light.\")\n",
    "        return 1 / np.sqrt(1 - (velocity / C) ** 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def decoherence_rate(energy, temperature=T_ZERO, velocity=0.0):\n",
    "        gamma_l = RelativisticDecoherence.lorentz_factor(velocity)\n",
    "        gamma_0 = ALPHA * abs(energy) / H_BAR\n",
    "        exponent = -abs(energy) / max(K_B * temperature * gamma_l, 1e-30)\n",
    "        return float(gamma_0 * gamma_l * np.exp(np.clip(exponent, -700, 0)))\n",
    "\n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def evolve_density_matrix(rho0, time_s, rate):\n",
    "        dim = rho0.shape[0]\n",
    "        mixed = np.eye(dim, dtype=np.complex128) / dim\n",
    "        decay = np.exp(-rate * time_s)\n",
    "        rho_t = decay * rho0 + (1 - decay) * mixed\n",
    "        return HilbertSpaceCorrection.enforce_hermiticity(rho_t)\n",
    "\n",
    "energy_expectation = float(abs(np.real(np.vdot(majorana_state, majorana_hamiltonian @ majorana_state))))\n",
    "energy_for_model = max(energy_expectation, 1e-24)\n",
    "velocity = 0.2 * C\n",
    "decoh_rate = RelativisticDecoherence.decoherence_rate(energy_for_model, T_ZERO, velocity)\n",
    "rho0 = np.outer(majorana_state, majorana_state.conj())\n",
    "time_grid = np.linspace(0, max(1e-6, 5 / max(decoh_rate, 1e-12)), 200)\n",
    "purities = []\n",
    "coherences = []\n",
    "for t in time_grid:\n",
    "    rho_t = RelativisticDecoherence.evolve_density_matrix(rho0, t, decoh_rate)\n",
    "    purities.append(np.real(np.trace(rho_t @ rho_t)))\n",
    "    coherences.append(np.sum(np.abs(rho_t - np.diag(np.diag(rho_t)))))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Energy used by toy model:\", energy_for_model)\n",
    "print(\"Lorentz factor:\", RelativisticDecoherence.lorentz_factor(velocity))\n",
    "print(\"Decoherence rate:\", decoh_rate)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Classical Q-learning state conditioner\n",
    "\n",
    "The agent learns among four actions: normalize, Hermitianize, perturb, or do nothing. This is classical tabular Q-learning operating on a quantum-inspired matrix representation.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class QuantumQAgent:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, actions=None, learning_rate=0.15, discount=0.9,\n",
    "                 epsilon=0.8, epsilon_decay=0.97, seed=SEED):\n",
    "        self.actions = actions or [\"normalize\", \"hermitianize\", \"perturb\", \"nothing\"]\n",
    "        self.lr = learning_rate\n",
    "        self.discount = discount\n",
    "        self.epsilon = epsilon\n",
    "        self.epsilon_decay = epsilon_decay\n",
    "        self.rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n",
    "        self.q_table = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "    def state_key(self, state):\n",
    "        norm = np.linalg.norm(state.ravel())\n",
    "        hermitian_error = (np.linalg.norm(state - state.conj().T)\n",
    "                           if state.ndim == 2 and state.shape[0] == state.shape[1] else 1.0)\n",
    "        finite = float(np.isfinite(state).all())\n",
    "        return (round(norm, 1), round(hermitian_error, 1), finite)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def choose_action(self, key):\n",
    "        self.q_table.setdefault(key, np.zeros(len(self.actions)))\n",
    "        if self.rng.random() < self.epsilon:\n",
    "            return int(self.rng.integers(len(self.actions)))\n",
    "        return int(np.argmax(self.q_table[key]))\n",
    "\n",
    "    def apply_action(self, state, action, step):\n",
    "        result = state.astype(np.complex128, copy=True)\n",
    "        if action == \"normalize\":\n",
    "            result = HilbertSpaceCorrection.normalize_hilbert(result)\n",
    "        elif action == \"hermitianize\":\n",
    "            result = HilbertSpaceCorrection.enforce_hermiticity(result)\n",
    "        elif action == \"perturb\":\n",
    "            rows, cols = result.shape\n",
    "            x, y = np.meshgrid(np.arange(rows), np.arange(cols), indexing=\"ij\")\n",
    "            wave = 0.03 * (np.cos(PI / PHI * x + 0.1 * step)\n",
    "                           + 1j * np.sin(E / SQRT2 * y + 0.1 * step))\n",
    "            result = result + wave\n",
    "        return result\n",
    "\n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def quality(state):\n",
    "        norm_error = abs(np.linalg.norm(state.ravel()) - 1.0)\n",
    "        hermitian_error = np.linalg.norm(state - state.conj().T) / state.size\n",
    "        invalid_penalty = 100.0 if not np.isfinite(state).all() else 0.0\n",
    "        return -(norm_error + hermitian_error + invalid_penalty)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def train(self, initial_state, episodes=80, max_steps=20):\n",
    "        episode_rewards, final_norms, final_hermitian_errors = [], [], []\n",
    "        best_state = initial_state.copy()\n",
    "        best_quality = self.quality(best_state)\n",
    "        for _ in range(episodes):\n",
    "            state = initial_state.copy()\n",
    "            total_reward = 0.0\n",
    "            for step in range(max_steps):\n",
    "                key = self.state_key(state)\n",
    "                action_index = self.choose_action(key)\n",
    "                next_state = self.apply_action(state, self.actions[action_index], step)\n",
    "                reward = self.quality(next_state) - self.quality(state)\n",
    "                next_key = self.state_key(next_state)\n",
    "                self.q_table.setdefault(next_key, np.zeros(len(self.actions)))\n",
    "                old = self.q_table[key][action_index]\n",
    "                target = reward + self.discount * np.max(self.q_table[next_key])\n",
    "                self.q_table[key][action_index] = old + self.lr * (target - old)\n",
    "                state = next_state\n",
    "                total_reward += reward\n",
    "                if self.quality(state) > best_quality:\n",
    "                    best_quality, best_state = self.quality(state), state.copy()\n",
    "            self.epsilon = max(0.02, self.epsilon * self.epsilon_decay)\n",
    "            episode_rewards.append(total_reward)\n",
    "            final_norms.append(np.linalg.norm(state.ravel()))\n",
    "            final_hermitian_errors.append(np.linalg.norm(state - state.conj().T))\n",
    "        return best_state, {\"reward\": episode_rewards, \"norm\": final_norms,\n",
    "                            \"hermitian_error\": final_hermitian_errors}\n",
    "\n",
    "q_agent = QuantumQAgent()\n",
    "trained_state, q_history = q_agent.train(initial_quantum_state)\n",
    "print(\"Initial quality:\", q_agent.quality(initial_quantum_state))\n",
    "print(\"Best quality:\", q_agent.quality(trained_state))\n",
    "print(\"Best-state validation:\", HilbertSpaceCorrection.state_validity_check(trained_state))\n",
    "print(\"Q-table states:\", len(q_agent.q_table))\n"
   ]
  },
