   "source": [
    "## Interpretation and limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "- The VAE is a real machine-learning model trained on a synthetic dataset.\n",
    "- The Majorana operators use a standard Pauli/Jordan-Wigner-style construction, but the chosen Hamiltonian and dataset are educational examples.\n",
    "- The decoherence equation is an illustrative software model, not an experimentally calibrated law.\n",
    "- The Q-learning agent is classical. It manipulates a quantum-inspired state representation but does not execute on quantum hardware.\n",
    "- Scaling this notebook to one million qubits is not computationally feasible with dense state vectors because the Hilbert-space dimension grows exponentially.\n"
   ]
